Root of Trust

A Root of Trust (RoT) is a foundational, inherently trusted hardware or software component that ensures system security by providing a secure starting point for cryptographic operations, secure boot, and verification. It acts as a trusted anchor, often a chip, that safeguards cryptographic keys and measurements, preventing unauthorized access and detecting tampering.

https://trustedcomputinggroup.org/about/what-is-a-root-of-trust-rot/

